# `later` is copied into the loop behind a guard on its arguments. Records out of JSON.parse are not of the written layout, so every call leaves for the slow body, which is written straight.
# Its callers lean on what it returns (number|bigint), so it holds its answer to that type. A type that is more than one word's test was asked of the run time: a call into C++ for every return, about eighty instructions.
# Where every number passes the type, the word is asked for a number first; the run time is asked for what is none (the big integers of the third answer).
# -- source: a-slow-body-tells-a-number-by-its-word-before-it-asks-the-run-time-for-the-type-of-what-it-returns.ts
